# SPEC-017: the marketing site uploads, and therefore serves, ONLY what is listed here.
# Vercel serves every uploaded file of this static project, so this file is the public
# surface. Everything at the root is excluded first, then the public paths are re-included.
# Enforced by tests/public-surface.test.mjs. Docs: vercel.com/docs/deployments/vercel-ignore
#
# The portal (Root Directory `app`) has its own app/.vercelignore. Vercel uses a project's
# own file in preference to this one, so this allowlist never applies to the portal build.

/*

# Generated pages and the deploy config (built by build.mjs).
!*.html
!vercel.json
!robots.txt
!sitemap.xml
!llms.txt

# Front-end runtime.
!css
!js
!assets

# Serverless functions, and the shared modules they import at runtime.
# api/intake.mjs imports src/data/site.mjs, so src/data (public business facts)
# and src/lib must upload. They are therefore readable at /src/data/*.mjs, which
# exposes nothing the rendered pages do not already show. Templates, styles and
# everything else under src/ stay out.
!api
!src
/src/*
!src/data
!src/lib

# Never upload, even inside an allowed directory.
.env*
.DS_Store
*.log
